.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wordCount
reads the file stream specified by
.I file
and counts its lines, words, and characters.
.PP
The resulting counts are stored in the integer variables pointed to by
.IR lines ,
.IR words ,
and
.IR chars .
The file stream must already be open.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns 0 on success and -1 if an error occurs.
